g.\\n- **`asyncpg`**: While the actual tests use a fake pool, the type hints and repository implementations rely on `asyncpg`.\\n- **Application Modules**: Tests import various modules from the application (e.g., `app.main`, `app.db.repositories`, `app.models`, `app.services`) to test their integration and individual functionality.\\n\\n## Notable Code Snippets\\n\\n### `tests/conftest.py` - `client` fixture:\\n```python\\n@pytest.fixture\\nasync def client(initialized_app: FastAPI) -> AsyncClient:\\n    async with AsyncClient(\\n        app=initialized_app,\\n        base_url="http://testserver",\\n        headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"},\\n    ) as client:\\n        yield client\\n```\\nThis fixture provides an `AsyncClient` instance that can be used to send requests to the FastAPI application during tests.\\n\\n### `tests/fake_asyncpg_pool.py` - `FakeAsyncPGPool`:\\n```python\\nclass FakeAsyncPGPool:\\n    # ... (implementation details)\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    async def create_pool(cls, pool: Pool) -> "FakeAsyncPGPool":\\n        pool = cls(pool)\\n        conn = await pool._pool.acquire()\\n        tx = conn.transaction()\\n        await tx.start()\\n        pool._conn = conn\\n        pool._tx = tx\\n        return pool\\n    # ... (rest of the implementation)\\n```\\nThis class mocks the behavior of `asyncpg.Pool` to provide a controllable database connection for tests.\\n\\n## Extension Points\\n\\n- New API tests can be added to `tests/test_api/`.\\n- New database-related tests can be added to `tests/test_db/`.\\n- New service logic tests can be added to `tests/test_services/`.\\n- The `conftest.py` file can be extended with more fixtures to support new testing scenarios.\\n- The `fake_asyncpg_pool.py` could be further enhanced to simulate more complex database behaviors if needed.\\n\\n## Related Tests\\n\\n- `tests/test_api/` contains tests for API routes.\\n- `tests/test_db/` contains tests for database interactions.\\n- `tests/test_schem